<article class="env-corollary" id="025E">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/025E">Corollary <span data-tag="025E">11.9.8.6</span>.</a> Let $\pi : \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \Delta ^ n$ be a cocartesian fibration of $\infty $-categories having fibers $\{  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(i) = \{ i\}  \times _{\Delta ^ n} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\} _{0 \leq i \leq n}$, and let </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ U: M( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(0) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(1) \rightarrow \cdots \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(n) ) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}. \]
</div>
<p> be a scaffold of $\pi $. Then, for every morphism of simplicial sets $X \rightarrow \Delta ^ n$, the induced map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  U': X \times _{\Delta ^ n} M( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(0) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(1) \rightarrow \cdots \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(n) ) \rightarrow X \times _{\Delta ^ n} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}} \]
</div>
<p> is a categorical equivalence of simplicial sets. </p>
</article>
